==Development==
''The Princess and the Scoundrel'' was known as "Misbehaving" during production.<ref name="Production">{{PenguinRandomHouse|url=books/706293/misbehaving-by-ballantine|text=Misbehaving By Ballantine}}</ref> The book was announced by [[StarWars.com]] on [[February 14]], [[2022]].<ref name="Reveal">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-princess-and-the-scoundrel|text=You're Invited to Han and Leia's Wedding in ''Star Wars: The Princess and the Scoundrel'' &ndash; Exclusive Reveal}}</ref>

While the first hardcover book to hold the logo was [[The High Republic: The Battle of Jedha (script)|''The High Republic: The Battle of Jedha'']],<ref name="Hoeler 1">{{Twitter|DarthInternous|status/1615883966011277312|[[Tom Hoeler]]|date=2023-01-19|quote=My pleasure. the copyright pages/logos will start being updated this year too. Princess and the Scoundrel's paperback will be the first book overall with the new logo. Battle of Jedha will be the first hardcover with it.|archivedate=20230314234431}}</ref> the paperback edition of ''The Princess and the Scoundrel'' is the first book to bear the "[[Random House Worlds]]" imprint on its spine and copyright page, according to [[Del Rey]] senior editor [[Tom Hoeler]].<ref name="Hoeler 2">{{Twitter|DarthInternous|status/1620452851347775489|[[Tom Hoeler]]|date=2023-03-31|quote=For historical note, THIS is the first book with "Random House Worlds" on the spine / copyright page. Battle of Jedha will be the first hardcover title, but Princess & Scoundrel paperback is the first book overall.|archivedate=20230131161937}}</ref>

